(4620825, 662132, 66201, '<td valign="top">Vastly underrated.... But I think you have won a few fans with this one :-)</td>', 'Vastly underrated.... But I think you have won a few fans with this one :-)', '2008-04-07 12:01:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4621835, 660999, 3746, '<td valign="top">congrats on a pretty good finish for your first entry! Its a good shot that meets the challenge well.. However, I am known for being critical so I don''t want to disappoint you here by being too nice..<br/> <br/>OK, the weakest point in this photo for me is the B&amp;W conversion. Just desaturating or converting to grayscale generally will result in a pretty flat image that can drain any life out of the image. Your best best would be to learn how to use the channel mixer to make some of the tones deeper and richer.. its hard to explain but channel mixed B&amp;Ws just have more depth and are tonally more pleasing.. if you need any advice on how to do that then feel free to drop me a line.<br/> <br/>Anyway, well done and hope to see more from you in the future.<br/> <br/>Mark.<br/> <br/>PS, tell Gloda to pull his finger out and arrange the Canterbury GTG.</td>', 'congrats on a pretty good finish for your first entry! Its a good shot that meets the challenge well.. However, I am known for being critical so I don''t want to disappoint you here by being too nice.. OK, the weakest point in this photo for me is the B&W conversion. Just desaturating or converting to grayscale generally will result in a pretty flat image that can drain any life out of the image. Your best best would be to learn how to use the channel mixer to make some of the tones deeper and richer.. its hard to explain but channel mixed B&Ws just have more depth and are tonally more pleasing.. if you need any advice on how to do that then feel free to drop me a line. Anyway, well done and hope to see more from you in the future. Mark. PS, tell Gloda to pull his finger out and arrange the Canterbury GTG.', '2008-04-07 19:55:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4623125, 662120, 70661, '<td valign="top">Kevin, this is so beautiful! Congrats on the great score and the upcoming addition to your family!</td>', 'Kevin, this is so beautiful! Congrats on the great score and the upcoming addition to your family!', '2008-04-08 06:44:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4624027, 661577, 84124, '<td valign="top">This is probably my favorite photo that I''ve viewed on this site.  I''m very surprised it didn''t ribbon.  Everything about this shot is so naturally captivating.  A testament to how good this shot is is if you look at my other favs, this is nothing like them, you drew me well out of my comfort zone with this, i.e. I didn''t even know I could like a shot like this.</td>', 'This is probably my favorite photo that I''ve viewed on this site.  I''m very surprised it didn''t ribbon.  Everything about this shot is so naturally captivating.  A testament to how good this shot is is if you look at my other favs, this is nothing like them, you drew me well out of my comfort zone with this, i.e. I didn''t even know I could like a shot like this.', '2008-04-08 14:25:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4624117, 661728, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>Congrats on a top 20.  This is a very nicely done shot and it meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Compositionally, it is well balanced, I think, between your two subjects.  You also fill the frame nicely so that there is not a lot of distracting background.  I do find having just the tip of his head cut off, when none of her''s is, a bit distracting, but nothing terribly important.<br/> <br/>Technically, the focus is great and the "colors" per se, are good.  There is a good range of blacks and grays.  In looking at it, my eyes try to make the shirt white.  I''m thinking his shirt is a colored one, and that will prevent it from being white.  I am by no means a craftful BW person, but in looking at the *really really really* good ones, there will be some definite black and some definite whites.  Also, the rose is almost un-noticeable.  In color, it would probably really add (though I think BW was an EXCELLENT choice), but in bw, it kinda fades away, and at first glance, I thought it was another arm from somewhere.  Perhaps if he had been stroking her face as she was his. . .<br/> <br/>Still, a great shot. <br/> <br/>If I need to further clarify anything, please feel free to contact me.<br/> <br/>karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat Congrats on a top 20.  This is a very nicely done shot and it meets the challenge well. Compositionally, it is well balanced, I think, between your two subjects.  You also fill the frame nicely so that there is not a lot of distracting background.  I do find having just the tip of his head cut off, when none of her''s is, a bit distracting, but nothing terribly important. Technically, the focus is great and the "colors" per se, are good.  There is a good range of blacks and grays.  In looking at it, my eyes try to make the shirt white.  I''m thinking his shirt is a colored one, and that will prevent it from being white.  I am by no means a craftful BW person, but in looking at the *really really really* good ones, there will be some definite black and some definite whites.  Also, the rose is almost un-noticeable.  In color, it would probably really add (though I think BW was an EXCELLENT choice), but in bw, it kinda fades away, and at first glance, I thought it was another arm from somewhere.  Perhaps if he had been stroking her face as she was his. . . Still, a great shot.  If I need to further clarify anything, please feel free to contact me. karma', '2008-04-08 15:26:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4624478, 661577, 62318, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot.</td>', 'Wonderful shot.', '2008-04-08 18:36:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4627245, 661445, 9462, '<td valign="top">So passionate, I''m jealous.<br/> <br/>The overexposure comments are funny.</td>', 'So passionate, I''m jealous. The overexposure comments are funny.', '2008-04-09 13:48:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4629825, 662258, 8367, '<td valign="top">Love this...you''ve captured their character. Excellent!</td>', 'Love this...you''ve captured their character. Excellent!', '2008-04-10 10:56:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4629859, 662258, 92402, '<td valign="top">very nice bw love the tones . made it fave I love it very much</td>', 'very nice bw love the tones . made it fave I love it very much', '2008-04-10 11:10:58.000000', NULL, 0);
